[71.59233, "o", "=== FIREWALL FIX SUMMARY ===\r\n\r\nPROBLEM IDENTIFIED:\r\n1. Rule ordering issue in rules.conf - deny rule for 10.80.0.0/16 came BEFORE allow rule for 10.80.4.0/24\r\n2. apply.sh was in dry-run mode and only logged commands without executing them\r\n\r\nFIXES APPLIED:\r\n1. Reordered rules.conf so monitoring allow rule (10.80.4.0/24 port 9100) comes BEFORE deny rule (10.80.0.0/16)\r\n2. Modified apply.sh to execute iptables commands instead of just logging them\r\n\r\nRESULT: Prometheus scrapes from 10.80.4.0/24 on port 9100 will now be allowed\r\n"]
